#|
Music can be understood, in the broadest sense, as modulated time 
— distinct from linear, chronometric time. While the latter 
generates predictable events, a great deal of music consists 
of varied temporal shapes. 

This lecture explores the relationships between stochastic 
musical processes and their perceptual qualities. 
|#

;;; 1.

;; chromatic scale in MIDI
;; linearity = determination
(setf chrom-scale (gen-integer 40 100))

(cons 's (midi-to-pitch chrom-scale))

;;; 2.

;; chromatic scale with small deviations
(setf chr-dev2
      (gen-loop 5 (midi-to-pitch
                   (gen-deviation
                    chrom-scale
                    ;; small deviation
                    -2 2))
                :seed 123))

;; low dissolution of direction, 
;; gradual ambiguity around a determinate centre.
(flatten (cons 's chr-dev2))

;;; 3.

;; chromatic scale with higher deviations
(setf chr-dev5
      (gen-loop 5 (midi-to-pitch
                   (gen-deviation
                    chrom-scale
                    ;; small deviation
                    -5 5))
                :seed 123))

;; stronger dissolution of direction 
;; -> increase of randomness inversely 
;; proportional to gestalt formation.
(flatten (cons 's chr-dev5))

;;; 4.

;; reduced tempo -> dissolution of the tendency, 
;; pitch shapes tend towards momentary form
(flatten (cons 'e chr-dev5))



;;; 5.

;; in quarter tempo and with higher deviations
;; direction is almost not perceptible

(setf chr-dev15
      (gen-loop 5
                (midi-to-pitch
                 (gen-deviation
                  (gen-integer 40 100)
                  -15 15))))

;;; 6.

;; higher speed (4 times faster), same pitches
;; -> tendency becomes audible again 
;; -> speed compensates for the effects of chance.
(flatten (cons 't chr-dev15))

;;; 7.

;; rhythmic deviations 
(setf length-dev1
      (vector-map '(1/16 1/8 1/4)
                  (rndn (length (flatten chr-dev15)) 
                        50 400 :seed 123)))

;; -> Gestalt (direction) is additionately dissolved 
;; by the unpredictability of the rhythmic structure.
(make-omn
 :pitch (flatten chr-dev15)
 :length length-dev1
 :velocity '(p))

;;; 8.

;; higher deviations from the repetition
(setf length-dev2
      (vector-map '(1/32 1/16 1/8 1/4 3/8 1/2)
                  (rndn (length (flatten chr-dev15)) 
                        50 400 :seed 123)))

;; increasingly dissolve the direction tendency
 (ps 'gm
     :treble (list (make-omn
                    :pitch (flatten chr-dev15)
                    :length length-dev2
                    :velocity '(p)))
     :time-signature '(4 4) 
     :tempo 60)